  "method": "Alternate before/after order each round; start one fresh daemon per sample. Hold every slot, issue DENY, observe the last stale FD's size becoming zero, then await the reply after replacement prefaults finish.",
  "limitations": [
    "Single-host control-plane benchmark; no claim about SQL or memory traversal speed.",
    "Observer polls fstat in Python and consumes one CPU while waiting; scheduling and IPC overhead are included in both variants.",
    "The last-FD timing measures its size becoming zero; DENY still replies only after refilling.",
    "Timed leases hold FDs without client mmap views. The observer detects file size zero, not the completion of TLB invalidation in arbitrary client mappings.",
    "THP remains a hint. Initial observed backing is recorded for each sample."
  ],
